From fbeeb79e67e44595de57a85cc5d70a26394dfc4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 07:44:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Source-agnostic ingestion: Wikisource support, derived
 available_languages, integrity checks

Fixes AN.KI's original-language ingestion gap (regression case: anna-karenina had
en/fi/nl editions but no ru original despite original_language=ru, while
available_languages falsely listed ru).

- omnia-ingest: dispatches on sourceId (gutenberg | wikisource) instead of
  rejecting everything but Gutenberg. New ingestFromWikisource() fetches the full
  work from the correct language Wikisource, normalizes to anki-json, requires an
  explicit workId (never creates a new Work), and asserts source/jurisdiction-
  specific rights (DE life+70, US published>=96y) instead of copying Gutenberg's
  public-domain/US. Gutenberg path is behavior-preserved.
- anki-multilingual-runner: source-agnostic candidate selection/processing
  (was hardcoded to source_id="gutenberg", starving every Wikisource candidate);
  reads back the real rights status per edition instead of asserting one.
- anki-multilingual-discover: fallback identity resolution for works with no
  master_corpus_candidates QID -- resolves via the author's Wikisource page +
  linked-page Wikidata classification, high-confidence single match only,
  ambiguous/failed lookups surface in fallbackIdentityUnresolved for review.
- available_languages_source_of_truth.sql: available_languages becomes a derived
  cache (compute_qualifying_languages / sync_work_available_languages) kept in
  sync by triggers on editions/book_files/rights_assertions, with a one-time
  repair of previously-stale rows.
- integrity_check_violations.sql: permanent check for missing_original_ready,
  stale_cached_language, ready_candidate_without_edition,
  ready_edition_without_usable_file, edition_attached_to_wrong_work.

